    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0056" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/5–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Hanoi</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >O’Sullivan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hanoi</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-21T13:00:00+07:00">May 21, 1946—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 22—1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Foreign Minister Nyugen Tuong Tarn today informed me he expected negotiations
                    would commence about June 15 and he thought they would last about 20 days.</p>
                <p>Tam indicated that Vietnamese delegation might be composed of as many as 30
                    persons. He said that personnel had not yet been decided upon but that it was
                    possible Ho Chi Minh might head mission.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept; repeated Nanking, Saigon informed airmail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Sullivan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
